.TH AET 1 "2026-11-15" "aeternus 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aet \- control a running Aeternus instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aet
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aet
talks to the most recently focused
.BR aeternus (1)
window on the current display through a Unix socket in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the Aeternus version into the active terminal.
.TP
.B pref
Open the Preferences panel.
.TP
.B reload
Reload config.toml.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the aet version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when no instance answered or the command failed, 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aeternus (1)
